//Constructor and Destructor in Inheritance

When inheritance is used, constructors and destructors are called in a specific order.

Constructor order

Parent constructor → Child constructor

class Parent {
public:
    Parent() {
        cout << "Parent";
    }
};

class Child : public Parent {
public:
    Child() {
        cout << "Child";
    }
};
Child obj;

Output:

ParentChild

So the parent is constructed first, then the child.

Destructor order

The opposite happens:

Child destructor → Parent destructor

~Child()
↓
~Parent()

So remember:

Constructor: Parent → Child
Destructor: Child → Parent

That's the important part of this topic.